      "sourceTextSha256": "32f7c4d431bc2cc4d8c0295c92af7f108d605e0a81f339698afeb2a74b380457",
      "text": "Day 10 · Breakfast and tour of the “White City”: the colonial district of San Lázaro, where Arequipa was founded, the Carmen Alto viewpoint over the Misti, Chachani and Pichu Pichu volcanoes, Yanahuara and its Andalusian-style church and ignimbrite arches, the Santa Catalina Monastery, closed to the public for nearly 400 years, the Plaza de Armas with the Cathedral, and the 17th-century Jesuit Church with its painted dome of St Ignatius. At 13:30, sleeper bus to Nazca (lunch and drinks included), founded by the Spanish in 1591 in the coastal desert famous for its giant geoglyphs. Transfer to the hotel.",
